cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhenoSuite in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "PhenoSuite: An Integrated Platform for Single-Cell Spatial Omics Analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Esteva
    given-names: Eduardo
    affiliation: "Translational Immunology Center (TrIC), New York University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/e-esteva/phenosuite"
url: "https://github.com/e-esteva/phenosuite"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - spatial-omics
  - single-cell
  - multiplexed-imaging
  - CODEX
  - PhenoCycler
  - MERFISH
  - spatial-transcriptomics
  - bioinformatics
  - R-Shiny
date-released: "2026-03-20"
abstract: >-
  PhenoSuite is an integrated bioinformatics platform for single-cell
  spatial omics analysis, built on R Shiny. Developed by the Translational
  Immunology Center (TrIC) at NYU, it provides modular tools for
  multiplexed immunofluorescence imaging (CODEX/PhenoCycler), spatial
  transcriptomics (MERFISH), cellular phenotyping, spatial interaction
  analysis, and multi-modal data integration. The entire platform ships
  as a single Docker image.
